    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26422" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δῐδῠμαῖος</span></b> , ὁ, a
		name of Zeus as worshipped at Didyma in Miletus jointly with Apollo, <i><span class="en">
			Nic.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			1
		</span></i>; of Apollo, <i><span class="en">
			<u>SIG</u>
			906
		</span></i>
        <u>A</u> (so <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δῐδῠμεύς</span></b> , ὁ, of Apollo, <i><span class="en">
			Orph.
			<u>H.</u>
			34.7
		</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ Διδυμαῖον,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>their temple</i> at Miletus,
				<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pomp.</u>
				24
			</span></i>:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δῐδύμεια</span></b> , τά, <i>their
			festival</i> there, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				2881
			</span></i>, al. (<span class="entity">Branchidae</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.129.8
			</span></i>.</div>
